{
    desc => q{j preserves virtual column across short lines},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/j_preserves_virtual_col`

Tests that `j` preserves the desired column when moving from a long line to a shorter line. The cursor clamps to the end of the short line but retains the virtual column for subsequent moves.

Keys: `$` → `j`

- **j_preserves_virtual_col_initial.png**: Cursor at line 1, col 0 on `a`
- **j_preserves_virtual_col_at_eol.png**: Cursor at line 1, col 29 on `e` (end of long line)
- **j_preserves_virtual_col_on_short.png**: Cursor at line 2, col 1 on `y` (clamped to end of short line "xy")
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('$');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('at_eol');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('j');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('on_short');
    },
}
__DATA__
a very long line of text here
xy
another very long line of text here
